# Each turn boxes the counter, one addition, and calls one stub with the set and the key in registers. The answer is a boolean in the lowest bit: one mask, one branch.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[wide]] = ZExt32(b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[key]] = Add(b@[[wide]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Int64 b@[[found]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@[[key]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Int32 b@[[low]] = Trunc(b@[[found]], {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[bit]] = BitAnd(b@[[low]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[bit]], Terminal)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The stub and the poll of the loop are all that can leave the loop.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# CALLS: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS: isLoopPoll, ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
